@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-controls-use-native-feedback
Shared controls MUST retain the existing cue vocabulary and role-to-cue selection.
A host MUST install its native feedback adapter before presenting interactive shared
controls. Audio, haptics and their user/system settings MUST remain native services;
shared controls MUST NOT supply a silent substitute. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
maximum-reuse iOS decision; DESIGN.md rules 109 and 120, J20.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-feedback-is-a-completed-activation
A control cue MUST play only when activation commits, before its action callback.
Scrolling away from a pressed control MUST remain silent. A hold MUST use the native
adapter's existing hold effect and MUST disable Compose's independent default buzz.
Source: existing CueModifiers behavior retained by the 21 Oct iOS decision; J20.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-cuelume-keeps-existing-synthesis
Android and iOS MUST use the same existing Cuelume recipes, cue shaping, synthesis
and mixer behavior. Native adapters MAY provide workers, synchronization, resource
loading, PCM output and system haptics; they MUST NOT substitute generic sounds or
change the cues' signatures and tempos. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS
decision, DESIGN.md rules 109, 120 and 125, and the existing Cuelume browser goldens.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] shared-control-sounds-stay-dry
A tap, select or toggle MUST retain the existing dry Default material click and
knock; ringing notes MUST remain outcomes rather than control activations. Turning
sound off MUST drop pending synthesis and fade voices already playing. Source:
DESIGN.md rule 125, J3/J16, and retained Android sound-no-ringing-controls behavior.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-gestures-retain-touch-only-roles
Sheet arrival/settlement, drag thresholds and page changes MUST retain their existing
native touch feedback roles and MUST NOT play an audible cue merely to obtain a haptic.
The installed host MUST implement those roles with the saved haptics preference and
system settings. Source: DESIGN.md rules 109 and 120, J12, and Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
maximum-reuse iOS decision.
